# tools/conic_paint_witness.rish -- a CONIC positioned gradient SEEN on a real image proves itself on metal (Season G).
#
# Season G (Open Media Primitives) -- the third and last shape of the CSS gradient triad, the sibling of
# tools/gradient_paint_witness.rish (the LINEAR family) and tools/radial_paint_witness.rish (the RADIAL circle). This rung
# proves the CONIC sweep: a pixel's ramp position is its bearing clockwise from the top, so the first control sits at the
# top and the ramp sweeps around, every ray from the center one constant wedge color (the CSS conic-gradient shape). Stands
# on the positioned ramp (image/color_ramp_stops.rye), the open color algebra (image/color.rye), and the open QOI codec
# (image/qoi.rye).
# Design read: active-designing/20260816-210735_season-g-color-algebra-crux.md (the color floor this stands on).
# Teacher, thanked clean-room: gratitude/w3c-css-color.md (the W3C CSS Color / Images specs -- public standards only).
#
# The crux this witness proves is that a conic positioned gradient becomes a real image: paint_gradient_conic fills a box
# where each pixel is the color the positioned ramp samples at its angular bearing. A black-to-white sweep makes each
# pixel's red channel equal its bearing, so the top reads 0, east 63, south 127, west 191 exactly (a clockwise quarter-turn
# per cardinal, the four ascending strictly); each ray from the center is one constant wedge color; the top is the seam
# where the first and last controls meet; a red-green-blue sweep round-trips through the open QOI codec byte-for-byte;
# uneven positions bend the sweep where even spacing cannot; a sub-rectangle paints only its own box; a non-square box still
# tops and seams exactly; a single-pixel box, a zero dimension, an out-of-bounds box, and a non-ascending ramp refuse by
# name having painted nothing. Compose not braid -- color_ramp_stops decides the color, qoi owns the target, color
# composites; this rung only routes each pixel to its angular bearing. The routing is integer fixed-point (a pseudo-angle,
# no trigonometry) so a sweep is deterministic. No network, no key, no funds.
#
# Run from the repository root:
#   rishi/bin/rishi run tools/conic_paint_witness.rish

say "conic-paint: Language EN -- Season G's conic positioned gradient painted onto an image; a keeper names a stop list and reads back a gradient sweep a surface can show, on our own color model and open codec."
say "conic-paint: Style Radiant -- compose not braid; color_ramp_stops DECIDES each pixel's color, qoi owns the RGBA target, color composites src-over, and this rung only ROUTES each pixel to its bearing clockwise from the top so a translucent sweep tints the picture beneath."
say "conic-paint: Lens TAME -- the whole box bound-checked ONCE up front in u64 so a far edge can never wrap; the ramp validated ONCE before any pixel so a malformed sweep refuses having painted nothing; the bearing routed through an integer pseudo-angle (no trigonometry) so a sweep is deterministic; no network, no key, no funds."

let zig = "vendor/zig-toolchain/zig"
let bin = "image/bin/conic_paint"

let build = run ["sh" "-c" "mkdir -p image/bin && env RYE_ZIG=${zig} rye/bin/rye build image/conic_paint.rye -femit-bin=${bin}"]
assert build.ok else "conic-paint: build failed -- ${build.err}"

let selftest = run ["sh" "-c" "${bin} selftest 2>&1"]
assert selftest.ok else "conic-paint: selftest exited non-zero -- ${selftest.out}"

let out = trim selftest.out
say "conic-paint: ${out}"

assert selftest.out contains "GREEN image-conic-paint" else "conic-paint: selftest did not print the GREEN conic-paint line"

assert selftest.out contains "round-trips through the open QOI codec byte-for-byte" else "conic-paint: the painted sweep did not prove its QOI round trip"

assert selftest.out contains "the sweep turns clockwise from the top by a quarter" else "conic-paint: the sweep did not prove its cardinal bearings turn clockwise"

assert selftest.out contains "each ray from the center is one constant wedge color" else "conic-paint: the sweep did not prove its rays are constant wedges"

assert selftest.out contains "bend the sweep where even spacing cannot" else "conic-paint: the sweep did not prove it bends with position"

say "conic-paint: GREEN -- a conic positioned gradient painted onto a real image, its top seam and cardinal bearings exact, its rays constant wedges, its bend measured, its round trip byte-for-byte, proven on metal."
